  1538	    // [way-2] SPLIT MASS TRACES AT CHROMATOGRAPHIC VALLEYS.
  1539	    // MassTraceDetection never splits at a local minimum: it terminates only on consecutive-miss
  1540	    // outliers or sample_rate, and max_trace_length only DISCARDS. So two peptides eluting 25 s apart
  1541	    // within the m/z tolerance merge into ONE multi-modal trace, whose XIC then correlates with
  1542	    // everything under it. ElutionPeakDetection is the OpenMS stage that actually smooths and splits
  1543	    // at local minima - we never ran it. width_filtering is forced to "off" because "fixed" is a
  1544	    // DELETION filter ([min_fwhm,max_fwhm]) and blanket deletion is on the falsified list.
  1545	    // [epd-parallel] Valley-splitting is the dominant serial phase (EPD-off S30 20:46 vs 28:40 for
  1546	    // MS2 alone). It is per-trace independent, so run it as a BALANCED parallel-for over the merged
  1547	    // traces -- more chunks than threads + dynamic schedule so no chunk's long traces stall the
  1548	    // rest. Lock-free (patched OpenMS), so the 8 concurrent windows above never contend. Trace SET
  1549	    // is identical to one serial split (per-trace, deterministic); only order differs, and both
  1550	    // consumers are order-independent (MS2 re-sorted after detectTraces_, MS1 sorted before
  1551	    // inferPrecursors_). Reverted once for a -0.8% "regression" that was actually the ms1_traces
