codex
One concrete set-changing defect is already visible: “membership” is only a predicate during candidate search, while emptiness is tested on the unfiltered slab. A frame containing only peaks at or below noise is empty to OpenMS but non-empty here, so this code counts a miss that OpenMS does not. I’m verifying the two omitted OpenMS details (counter updates and scan-count formula) against the upstream 3.x source before ranking the rest.
