./docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:32:  Also README build instructions: `build/DIAPseudoSpectra` but CMakeLists doesn't show how to build standalone beyond `cmake -DOpenMS_DIR=...`. README says "then rebuild the OpenMS DIAPseudoSpectra target" — contradictory with "standalone application, lives outside the OpenMS source tree"! The README Build section says apply patches to OpenMS and "rebuild the OpenMS DIAPseudoSpectra target" — but the tool is standalone per CMakeLists comment. That's an inconsistency worth flagging: the apply_openms_patches.sh installs src/TdfMzCalibration.h + patches into OpenMS; but where does DIAPseudoSpectra get built? CMakeLists exists for standalone. README never gives the actual cmake commands for building this repo. Gap.
./docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:116:  Env vars in code: SPEXTRACT_DROP_PREC_ISO, SPEXTRACT_MZ_ESTIMATOR, SPEXTRACT_DET, SPEXTRACT_PICK_SERIAL, SPEXTRACT_PICK_STATIC, SPEXTRACT_PICK_BATCH, SPEXTRACT_PICK_MZ_MODE, SPEXTRACT_LOAD_ONLY, SPEXTRACT_MIN_ISOTOPES, SPEXTRACT_PRECURSOR_LIST, SPEXTRACT_MZPEAK_EXACT, SPEXTRACT_MZPEAK_TDF, SPEXTRACT_ALLOW_CHORD_FALLBACK (in TdfMzCalibration.h presumably), SPEXTRACT_BACKFILL_RAW?, SPEXTRACT_ISO_COLLAPSE? Need grep.
./docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:120:  1. `SPEXTRACT_ISO_COLLAPSE` and `SPEXTRACT_BACKFILL_RAW` / `SPEXTRACT_BACKFILL_MAXFRAGS` are documented in CHANGELOG (Unreleased → "Added") but DO NOT EXIST in the source. Grep of getenv in src/ shows neither. So the CHANGELOG claims features that aren't in the code. That's a doc-vs-code inconsistency — maybe implemented elsewhere? Let me grep the whole src for "ISO_COLLAPSE" and "BACKFILL" to be sure (could be non-getenv via Param?). Also `SPEXTRACT_ALLOW_CHORD_FALLBACK` lives in TdfMzCalibration.h (src/TdfMzCalibration.h) — outside the two files but fine.
./docs/reviews/release-2026-09-03/kimi.err:248:  1. tests/test_calibration_cpp.cpp exists for the calibration header — but does CI test the main tool? .github/workflows/tests.yml exists per CHANGELOG. Q5 asks about unit tests for the tool itself: none. tests/ covers TdfMzCalibration + entrapment estimator only.
