   983	    /// [perf-load] Pick+compact a BATCH of buffered frames in parallel, then append in arrival
   984	    /// order. OpenMS hands frames over a strictly serial `for (fid..) consumeSpectrum(spec)` loop,
   985	    /// so before this the peak picking of 1.26e9 peaks ran on ONE thread and was 53% of total wall
   986	    /// (measured: 1046 s wall, parallel factor 1.0). Buffering here parallelises it without
   987	    /// touching the reader. Appending strictly by buffer index keeps the output order identical to
   988	    /// the serial path; the emitted spectra matched it in m/z and differed in ~2% of intensities at
   989	    /// the 1e-5..1e-4 relative level (Sage count unchanged) -- see docs/RUNTIME-PLAN [pick-det].
   990	    void flush_()
   991	    {
